  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the zombie as 'me'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the zombie visual entity, which is explicitly mapped as 'me' in the meme's text. The text 'gay people fear me' directly assigns the role of 'me' to the zombie, positioning the viewer as the feared entity. This projection is reinforced by the zombie's menacing posture and the framing of the scene, which places the zombie in a threatening, confrontational stance toward the viewer. The user is thus semiotically projected onto the zombie as the self ('me') in the context of the meme's false claim about homophobia.",
